# Events on the marsh track between Vallaki and Berez (data/random_encounters/berez_marsh.json).

~ drowned_bell
Narrator: Somewhere ahead, under the black water, a bell rings. Once, then again, slow, the way a chapel bell rings for a burial. There is no wind. There is no chapel.
interject tag:curious: Bells don't ring underwater. Do they? They shouldn't.
* Wade out toward the sound. -> bell_wade
* [Religion DC 13] Say a word for whoever it's ringing for. -> bell_prayer | bell_prayer_fail
* Keep to the track. -> bell_leave

~ bell_wade
time +20
Narrator: Thigh-deep in the cold, your boots find the bell where it fell: on its side in the silt, green with weed, its clapper still swinging. Wedged in the mouth of it, somebody's offerings from a long time ago, coins gone black.
gold +18
Narrator: When you let go of it, the bell stops. When you turn your back, it starts again.
-> END

~ bell_prayer
Narrator: The words go out over the water. The bell rings once more, softer, and stops, and does not start again. The marsh feels less crowded afterwards.
-> END

~ bell_prayer_fail
Narrator: The words go out over the water, and the bell rings straight through them, as if it has heard a great many prayers and none of them helped.
-> END

~ bell_leave
Narrator: You keep to the logs. The bell follows you for a while, always just ahead, and then gives up.
-> END

~ raven_guide
Narrator: A raven drops onto a post at the side of the track and looks at you with one eye, then the other, as if checking its arithmetic.
if flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met or flag.raven_fed
Narrator: It hops to the next post, and the next, and looks back each time. Following it, you skirt three pools that would have had you up to the neck, and a patch of reeds where something large turns over and goes back to sleep.
interject tag:cheerful: I'm going to start leaving out bread for every bird in this country.
-> END
endif
Narrator: It caws once, takes off, and circles, unconvinced. Ravens in Barovia are particular about whom they help, and you haven't been introduced.
* [Animal Handling DC 13] Hold out a crust and wait. -> raven_won | raven_lost
* Walk on. -> END

~ raven_won
Narrator: After a long, judging moment it takes the crust, and then leads you round the worst of the pools before it flies off east, toward the drowned village.
-> END

~ raven_lost
Narrator: It looks at the crust, looks at you, and leaves with an expression you didn't know a bird could make.
-> END
